---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { entity } from "../data/entity";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that govern your use of this website and your engagement with Global Book Publishing's services."
>
  <section class="bg-navy-900 text-offwhite-100">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">LEGAL</p>
      <h1 class="on-navy">Terms of Service</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-ivory-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 leading-relaxed">
      <div class="card p-5 border-dashed bg-gold-100 border-gold-500 mb-10">
        <p class="font-semibold">
          This is a draft starting point. Have a lawyer review this page before it governs real
          transactions. [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: legal review]
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">Last updated: [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: publish date]</p>

      <h2>Who these terms cover</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        These terms apply to anyone using this website, {entity.brandName}, operated by {entity.legalName}
        ({entity.legalNameShort}), and to anyone engaging {entity.legalNameShort} for book writing,
        publishing, marketing, or related services. Using this site or working with us means you accept
        these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">What this website is</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        This site provides information about writing and publishing a book, free resources like the Expert
        Book Blueprint and the newsletter, and a way to book a call or purchase services. Content on this
        site is general information, not a guarantee of any specific outcome for your book. See our
        <a href="/disclaimer" class="underline font-semibold">disclaimer</a> for the specifics on results and
        guarantees.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Services and separate agreements</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Any paid engagement (writing, publishing, marketing, or related services) is governed by its own
        signed agreement, which will spell out deliverables, timelines, pricing, and rights in detail. These
        general terms don't replace that agreement; where the two conflict, your signed service agreement
        controls. [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: link or reference to the standard service agreement template once
        finalized].
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Intellectual property</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        You keep 100% of the rights, royalties, and intellectual property in the book you write with us.
        Content on this website itself (the text, design, and resources we publish, like the Blueprint)
        belongs to {entity.legalNameShort} and may not be reproduced without permission.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Don't use this site to submit false information, attempt to compromise its security, or scrape its
        content for unauthorized reuse. Forms exist for real inquiries from real people.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">No guarantee of results</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Nothing on this site is a promise of income, sales, or any specific result for your book. Any
        revenue or results example described anywhere on this site is a description of what happened for us
        or a specific client, not a projection for you. The only guarantee that applies to any engagement is
        the specific, scoped guarantee described in writing on that service's own page and in your signed
        agreement, never a general promise of a "guaranteed bestseller." See the full
        <a href="/disclaimer" class="underline font-semibold">disclaimer</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: standard limitation-of-liability language, to be drafted or reviewed by
        counsel for your jurisdiction].
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Governing law</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        These terms are governed by the laws of {entity.address.region}, {entity.address.country}.
        [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: confirm final governing law and venue with counsel].
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Questions about these terms can go to {entity.contactEmail || "[NEEDS CONFIRMATION: legal contact email]"}
        or through our <a href="/contact" class="underline font-semibold">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
